\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
Pahanan Agta (ISO 639-3: apf; also called Paranan Agta or Palanan Agta) is spoken by a Negrito community in Palanan, Isabela, in the northern Philippines. Wikipedia gives about 1,700 speakers as of 2009. It is lexically very close to the unrelated-in-structure Paranan language. Few resources were found, and none designed for schools.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers, textbooks or school programmes were found in search results.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Overview of the language (encyclopedic, secondary source): \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paranan_Agta_language}
\item Glottolog family page, Paranan-Pahanan: \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/para1320}
\item Article in Oceanic Linguistics on the classification of the Northeastern Luzon languages: \url{https://muse.jhu.edu/article/511885}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Scripture Earth listing of Bible portions in the language (Gospels of Mark and Luke were listed): \url{https://scriptureearth.org/00eng.php?iso=apf}
\item Joshua Project people profile (secondary source, generic wording): \url{https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/20541}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Global Recordings Network language page: \url{https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/apf}
\end{itemize}
The Global Recordings page reported no recordings of its own; it mentions a 2016 New Testament available through Faith Comes By Hearing, but no direct URL for that was seen.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Material in the language appears limited to scripture portions. No dictionary, grammar or school material was found, so a curriculum would require new documentation work with the community.

\end{document}
